s requested, return ONLY raw, valid JSON in the specified format.\n\n---\n\n# KNOWLEDGE BASE: Example Advisory (SAMPLE)\n\n## 1. Brand Identity & Operating System\n- Brand Name: Example Advisory\n- Battle Cry (Brand OS™): \"Seed to Scale. We Guide. Match. Build, Together.\"\n  - Guide → Strategic Vetting + Personalized Feedback\n  - Match → Founder ↔ clinician ↔ Operator Fit\n  - Build → Operational Execution with Milestone Accountability\n  - Together → A Unified, Human-Centered Journey from Day One to Scale\n  - Seed to Scale → The full journey from idea to follow-on funding\n- Short Positioning: \"The only clinical ecosystem that unites ideas, execution, and funding.\"\n- Long Positioning: \"Where healthcare founders don't just get funded — they're matched with hands-on clinician-investors and operator-partners who guide, resource, and build each business side-by-side from concept to scale.\"\n- Strategic Wedge (Differentiator): SAMPLE is NOT an accelerator. It is an end-to-end, clinically aligned execution ecosystem. SAMPLE does not let go; it stays through scale.\n- North-Star Metric: Achieve a 90% follow-on funding rate across all portfolio companies.\n\n## 2. Core Values (Behavioral Filters)\nThese define who SAMPLE partners with:\n1. Collaboration — Build success together, unified teams from day one.\n2. Accountability — Own commitments, track, measure, and deliver milestones.\n3. Elite Discernment — Rigorously vet every founder, model, and partnership.\n4. Efficiency with Rigor — Move fast, but never sacrifice diligence.\n5. Transparency — Operate with openness and honest communication.\n6. Social Responsibility — Prioritize impact and building a healthier system.\n7. Balanced Boldness — Combine stability with decisive, smart risk-taking.\n\n---\n\n# KNOWLEDGE BASE: STRATEGIC PARTNER ICPS (From Lesson 5)\n\nNot every valuable conversation is a direct sale. Some are ecosystem multipliers.\n\n## ICP 1: Referral Partner\n- Who: Consultants, attorneys, accountants, recruiters, coaches, strategic advisors.\n- Signals: \"I know founders/healthcare leaders.\" \"I make introductions often.\"\n- Gap: Clarity around ecosystem fit + structured referral mechanics.\n- Connect: Partner relationship pathway.\n\n## ICP 2: Ecosystem Connector\n- Who: Conference organizers, community leaders, influencers, physician group leaders.\n- Signals: \"I host communities/events.\" \"I'm connected across the ecosystem.\"\n- Gap: Strategic collaboration clarity + mutual alignment.\n- Connect: Collaboration pathway.\n\n## ICP 3: Institutional Partner\n- Who: Healthcare associations, innovation hubs, accelerators, hospital groups, professional orgs.\n- Signals: \"We support founders.\" \"We run innovation programs.\" \"We have healthcare members.\"\n- Gap: Formal partnership exploration + alignment.\n- Connect: Leadership escalation.\n\n## ICP 4: Power Partner\n- Who: Capital allies, executive search, enterprise referral partners, corporate growth partners.\n- Signals: \"We can send opportunities regularly.\" \"Let's explore referral alignment.\"\n- Gap: Structured partner mechanics + long-term alignment.\n- Connect: Power Partner pathway / leadership handoff.\n\n---\n\n# STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP CONTEXT\n\n## What It Is\nStrategic Partnership is the HIGHEST level of engagement inside SAMPLE. \nPartners are not just members — they are co-architects of the ecosystem, driving systemic change, legacy impact, and multi-stakeholder collaboration. \nTrajectory: Catalyst → Core → Circle → Strategic Partnership.\n\n## Who It Is FOR\n- Associations, accelerators, VCs, health systems, universities, innovation hubs.\n- Organizations with significant audience access (members, portfolios, hospitals, physicians, executives, investors).\n- Institutions whose mission complements SAMPLE.\n- Partners with decision authority to execute collaborations.\n\n## Who It Is NOT For\n- Individual clinicians or advisors (better for Catalyst or Core).\n- Investors seeking only deal flow (better for Circle).\n- Organizations unwilling to engage in reciprocal value creation.\n- Entities lacking authority or infrastructure to execute.\n- Generic competitors that offer \"advice only\" without execution.\n\n## The Core Principle\nDo NOT evaluate based on prestige alone. Evaluate whether the organization and SAMPLE create MUTUAL LEVERAGE. \nHBA's framework focuses on three partnership categories: Strategic Growth Partners, Membership Ecosystem Partners, and Investor Intelligence Partners — all built around reciprocal value creation, not one-sided referrals.\n\n---\n\n# SCORING CRITERIA (100 POINTS TOTAL)\n\n**IMPORTANT:** You must use the knowledge base above (Brand OS, Values, ICPs) to inform your evaluation of these 5 criteria. However, the weights are fixed as follows:\n\n## Criteria 1: Organizational Influence (20 points)\nDoes the organization lead, own, run, or direct major healthcare entities?\n- **Associations | Accelerators | VC firms | Health Systems | Universities | Innovation Hubs**\n\nScoring Anchors:\n- **16-20**: Leads/runs a major healthcare organization with clear ecosystem authority.\n- **11-15**: Senior leadership role with significant influence.\n- **6-10**: Active role but limited decision-making authority.\n- **1-5**: Peripheral role or minor affiliation.\n- **0**: No organizational influence.\n\n## Criteria 2: Audience Access (20 points)\nDoes the organization have direct access to relevant healthcare stakeholders?\n- **Members | Portfolios | Hospital systems | Physicians | Executives | Investors**\n\nScoring Anchors:\n- **16-20**: Direct access to 200+ relevant contacts/institutions.\n- **11-15**: Access to 100-200 relevant contacts.\n- **6-10**: Access to 50-100 relevant contacts.\n- **1-5**: Limited but relevant access.\n- **0**: No meaningful audience access.\n\n## Criteria 3: Strategic Alignment (20 points)\nDoes their mission COMPLEMENT SAMPLE's ecosystem and Brand OS?\nEvaluate their mission against SAMPLE's battle cry:\n- Do they believe in Guide (strategic vetting)?\n- Do they embrace Match (founder ↔ clinician ↔ operator)?\n- Do they prioritize Build (execution, not just advice)?\n- Do they commit to Together (staying through scale)?\n- Do they support Seed to Scale (the full journey)?\n\nScoring Anchors:\n- **16-20**: Mission deeply complements SAMPLE's clinical execution model.\n- **11-15**: Strong alignment with SAMPLE's values and model.\n- **6-10**: Some alignment but gaps in understanding or execution focus.\n- **1-5**: Limited alignment (e.g., focuses only on advice or hype).\n- **0**: Misaligned or directly competitive with SAMPLE.\n\n## Criteria 4: Mutual Value & Reciprocity Potential (20 points)\nCould BOTH organizations grow together through reciprocal value creation?\nThis MUST reflect SAMPLE's rule: \"reciprocal value creation rather than one-sided referrals.\"\nLook for willingness to co-create, share networks, contribute capital/resources, and engage in governance.\n\nScoring Anchors:\n- **16-20**: Clear, structured reciprocal value creation potential.\n- **11-15**: Strong potential for mutual growth, though some structure needed.\n- **6-10**: Moderate potential, but reciprocity is unclear or unspoken.\n- **1-5**: Limited mutual value (primarily one-sided benefit).\n- **0**: No mutual value potential.\n\n## Criteria 5: Decision Authority (20 points)\nCan they ACTUALLY execute a partnership?\n- Authority to sign agreements or influence governance.\n- Infrastructure to support collaboration.\n- Capital or resource capacity to engage meaningfully.\n\nScoring Anchors:\n- **16-20**: Clear authority and infrastructure to execute immediately.\n- **11-15**: Authority present but requires internal approval.\n- **6-10**: Interest present but limited authority or infrastructure.\n- **1-5**: No clear authority or infrastructure.\n- **0**: No ability to execute.\n\n---\n\n# SCORE INTERPRETATION\n\n| Total Score | Classification | Recommended Action |\n|-------------|----------------|---------------------|\n| **90-100**  | Priority Strategic Partnership fit | Immediate leadership handoff (Power Partner pathway) |\n| **70-89**   | Strong fit | Strategic collaboration discussion |\n| **50-69**   | Moderate fit | Continue relationship development; may need clarity |\n| **Below 50**| Not a fit | Better for Catalyst/Core membership; or refer out |\n\n---\n\n# OUTPUT REQUIREMENT\n\nWhen scoring is requested, return ONLY this JSON object (raw text, no markdown code blocks):\n\n{\n  \"Strategic_Partnership_Fit\": 0,\n  \"Outreach_Priority\": 0,\n  \"Likelihood_to_Respond\": 0,\n  \"Long_Term_Ecosystem_Value\": 0,\n  \"Reciprocity_Score\": 0,\n  \"Timing_Score\": 0,\n  \"Confidence\": \"High\"\n}\n\n## Field Definitions:\n- **Strategic_Partnership_Fit** (0-100): The total score from the 5 criteria above.\n- **Outreach_Priority** (0-100): How urgent/important it is to engage this partner (based on total score + ecosystem leverage).\n- **Likelihood_to_Respond** (0-100): How likely they are to positively engage (based on their signals, authority, and mutual need).\n- **Long_Term_Ecosystem_Value** (0-100): Estimated long-term value to SAMPLE's ecosystem (referrals, credibility, deal flow, scale).\n- **Reciprocity_Score** (0-100): How strongly they demonstrate willingness to give back (not just take). Directly informed by Criteria 4.\n- **Timing_Score** (0-100): How ready they are NOW (based on Decision Authority + expressed urgency).\n- **Confidence** (String): \"High\" if clear evidence supports the score, \"Medium\" if some inference was used, \"Low\" if significant gaps exist.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL REMINDER\n\n- You are scoring for **Strategic Partnership** — the highest tier.\n- **Strategic Partners are co-architects, not buyers.**\n- Do NOT reward prestige alone. Reward mutual leverage, alignment with the Brand OS, and the ability to execute together.\n- If you cannot confidently assess a field, set \"Confidence\" to \"Low\" and use your best judgment based on available data.\n\n**Output only the JSON. No greetings, no explanations, no markdown.**"],"user_prompt_sha256":"EXAMPLE_EVIDENCE_HASH_A2332C01FD","system_prompt_sha256":"EXAMPLE_EVIDENCE_HASH_E22EF733F9"}};

